  2069	// Ring sanitization tolerances. Operator-recorded field boundaries carry
  2070	// mm-scale geometric degeneracies (a real 252 m² field had a 1.2 mm near-
  2071	// duplicate closure vertex and several 1–10 mm sliver edges). These are EXACT
  2072	// enough that boost::geometry accepts the points yet degenerate enough that
  2073	// F2C's generateHeadlands offset and BruteForce swath clip silently produce
  2074	// PARTIAL coverage. Both tolerances sit safely below op_width (0.16 m) so no
  2075	// real corner is ever removed.
