  2077	constexpr double kRingSpikeTolM = 0.005;  // drop a vertex within 5 mm of its neighbours' chord
  2078	
  2079	// Repair a ring into a boost::geometry-valid one via F2C's own OGR backend.
  2080	// Buffer-by-zero is the standard OGR self-intersection fix (the same Buffer call
  2081	// bufferRingOutward already relies on); it returns the valid equivalent of a
  2082	// self-touching / sliver-laden ring. Keep the largest resulting polygon's
  2083	// exterior. Any degeneracy (null buffer, empty result, collapsed ring) returns
  2084	// the input unchanged — the planner must NEVER drop the field.
